Feature: Product Sales Analysis Logic Updates

  Background:
    Given the product sales data is loaded from Unity Catalog schema purgo_playground
    And the following columns exist in the sales dataset: sales_amount, bonus_eligibility, performance_flag, product_perf_band
    And rep_summary is aggregated per rep with total_rep_sales

  Scenario Outline: Update Bonus Eligibility per Transaction
    Given a sales transaction with sales_amount <sales_amount>
    When the bonus eligibility logic is applied
    Then bonus_eligibility should be "<expected_bonus_eligibility>"

    Examples:
      | sales_amount | expected_bonus_eligibility |
      | 26000        | Yes                       |
      | 25000        | <existing_logic>          |
      | 24999        | <existing_logic>          |

  Scenario Outline: Update Performance Flag per Transaction
    Given a sales transaction with sales_amount <sales_amount>
    When the performance_flag logic is applied
    Then performance_flag should be "<expected_flag>"

    Examples:
      | sales_amount | expected_flag |
      | 9500         | High         |
      | 9001         | High         |
      | 9000         | Medium       |
      | 8000         | Medium       |
      | 7001         | Medium       |
      | 7000         | Low          |
      | 5000         | Low          |

  Scenario Outline: Update Product Performance Band per Transaction
    Given a sales transaction with sales_amount <sales_amount>
    When the product_perf_band logic is applied
    Then product_perf_band should be "<expected_band>"

    Examples:
      | sales_amount | expected_band |
      | 15000        | Excellent    |
      | 10001        | Excellent    |
      | 10000        | Good         |
      | 9000         | Good         |
      | 8001         | Good         |
      | 8000         | Moderate     |
      | 5001         | Moderate     |
      | 5000         | <existing_or_poor> |

  Scenario Outline: Add Rep Tier to rep_summary
    Given a rep_summary record with total_rep_sales <total_rep_sales>
    When the rep_tier logic is applied
    Then rep_tier should be "<expected_tier>"

    Examples:
      | total_rep_sales | expected_tier   |
      | 50000           | Platinum Plus   |
      | 45001           | Platinum Plus   |
      | 45000           | Platinum        |
      | 40000           | Platinum        |
      | 35001           | Platinum        |
      | 35000           | Gold            |
      | 30000           | Gold            |
      | 25001           | Gold            |
      | 25000           | Silver          |
      | 20000           | Silver          |

  Scenario: Display Final Output with Updated Columns
    Given all logic updates have been applied to the sales and rep_summary datasets
    When the final output is displayed
    Then the output should include the updated columns: bonus_eligibility, performance_flag, product_perf_band, rep_tier

  Scenario Outline: Validation - sales_amount Type
    Given a sales transaction with sales_amount value <sales_amount>
    When the logic is applied
    Then if sales_amount is not numeric, an error "sales_amount must be numeric" should be raised

    Examples:
      | sales_amount |
      | "abc"        |
      | null         |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - total_rep_sales Type
    Given a rep_summary record with total_rep_sales value <total_rep_sales>
    When the rep_tier logic is applied
    Then if total_rep_sales is not numeric, an error "total_rep_sales must be numeric" should be raised

    Examples:
      | total_rep_sales |
      | "xyz"           |
      | null            |

  Scenario: Validation - Missing Required Columns
    Given the sales dataset is missing the sales_amount column
    When the logic is applied
    Then an error "Missing required column: sales_amount" should be raised

  Scenario: Validation - Duplicate rep_summary Records
    Given rep_summary contains duplicate rep_id records
    When the rep_tier logic is applied
    Then an error "Duplicate rep_id found in rep_summary" should be raised

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Allowed Values for rep_tier
    Given a rep_summary record with calculated rep_tier value <rep_tier>
    When the output is displayed
    Then rep_tier should be one of ["Platinum Plus", "Platinum", "Gold", "Silver"]

    Examples:
      | rep_tier      |
      | Platinum Plus |
      | Platinum      |
      | Gold          |
      | Silver        |
      | "Diamond"     |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Allowed Values for performance_flag
    Given a sales transaction with calculated performance_flag value <performance_flag>
    When the output is displayed
    Then performance_flag should be one of ["High", "Medium", "Low"]

    Examples:
      | performance_flag |
      | High             |
      | Medium           |
      | Low              |
      | "Super"          |

  Scenario Outline: Validation - Allowed Values for product_perf_band
    Given a sales transaction with calculated product_perf_band value <product_perf_band>
    When the output is displayed
    Then product_perf_band should be one of ["Excellent", "Good", "Moderate", "<existing_or_poor>"]

    Examples:
      | product_perf_band |
      | Excellent         |
      | Good              |
      | Moderate          |
      | Poor              |

  Scenario: Error Path - Null sales_amount
    Given a sales transaction with sales_amount null
    When the logic is applied
    Then an error "sales_amount cannot be null" should be raised

  Scenario: Error Path - Null total_rep_sales
    Given a rep_summary record with total_rep_sales null
    When the rep_tier logic is applied
    Then an error "total_rep_sales cannot be null" should be raised

  Scenario: Error Path - Missing rep_summary
    Given rep_summary is missing from the dataset
    When the rep_tier logic is applied
    Then an error "rep_summary dataset not found" should be raised

  Scenario: Error Path - Display Output with Missing Columns
    Given the output is displayed without the updated columns
    When the output is validated
    Then an error "Output missing required columns: bonus_eligibility, performance_flag, product_perf_band, rep_tier" should be raised

# END
